                "text": "Analyse the examples:\nIn Example 1:\nTwo components of color 6:\nComponent 1:\n(2, 7), (3, 7), (3, 8).\nNotice:\n(2, 7) is adjacent to (3, 7).\n(3, 8) is adjacent to (3, 7).\nIt forms a corner / right triangle / \"L\" tromino or corner shape of size 3.\nThe corner vertex is at (3, 7).\nThe two arms extend: up to (2, 7) and right to (3, 8).\nWait, where is the added pixel?\nAdded pixel is at (1, 9)!\nWait:\nFrom (3, 7) to (2, 7) goes direction (-1, 0).\nFrom (3, 7) to (3, 8) goes direction (0, +1).\nVector sum: (-1, 1).\nWait, from (2, 7) and (3, 8), what is (1, 9)?\nFrom (3, 7) + 2*(-1, 1) = (1, 9)?\n(3, 7) + (-1, 1) = (2, 8). But (2, 8) is 0! (Wait, (3, 8) is present, (2, 7) is present).\nThe 2x2 bounding box of the corner is rows 2..3, cols 7..8.\nThe missing corner in this 2x2 box is (2, 8).\nThe added pixel is at (1, 9)!\nNotice: (1, 9) is diagonally away from (2, 8)!\nDirection: from (3, 7) (the corner of the L) through (2, 8) (the empty corner of the 2x2) is (-1, +1).\n(3, 7) -> (2, 8) -> (1, 9)!\nSo it steps along the diagonal defined by the corner:\nCorner at (3, 7), empty spot of 2x2 is (2, 8).\nThe next cell along this diagonal is (1, 9)!\nLet's check Component 2 in Example 1:\nCells at (7, 2), (8, 1), (8, 2).\n2x2 bounding box: rows 7..8, cols 1..2.\nThe corner vertex of the L is (8, 2).\nArms: (7, 2) [up], (8, 1) [left].\nEmpty spot of 2x2: (7, 1).\nDiagonal direction from (8, 2) through (7, 1) is (-1, -1).\nNext cell along this diagonal: (7, 1) + (-1, -1) = (6, 0)!\nAnd output has (6, 0) set to 6! Exactly!\n\nLet's check Example 2:\nComponent 1:\n(1, 4), (2, 3), (2, 4).\nCorner is at (2, 4).\nArms are at (1, 4) [up], (2, 3) [left].\nEmpty spot of 2x2: (1, 3).\nDirection: (-1, -1).\nNext cell along diagonal: (1, 3) + (-1, -1) = (0, 2)!\nOutput has (0, 2) set to 2! Exactly!\n\nComponent 2:\n(7, 3), (7, 4), (8, 4).\nCorner is at (7, 4).\nArms: (7, 3) [left], (8, 4) [down].\nEmpty spot of 2x2: (8, 3).\nDirection: (+1, -1).\nNext cell: (8, 3) + (+1, -1) = (9, 2)!\nOutput has (9, 2) set to 2! Exactly!\n\nSo the rule is:\nEach 3-pixel L-tromino (corner shape in a 2x2):\nLet the corner cell be C = (r_c, c_c).\nThe two arms are at A1 = (r_c + dr, c_c) and A2 = (r_c, c_c + dc) where dr, dc in {-1, 1}.\nThe empty cell in the 2x2 is E = (r_c + dr, c_c + dc).\nThe diagonal continuation is E + (dr, dc) = (r_c + 2*dr, c_c + 2*dc).\nSet this cell to the same color as the tromino!I am ready for the test input.",
